WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:13.390
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:12.830
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.400
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.510
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.650
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.210
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.400
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:46.470
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:51.560
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.600
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.530
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:12.980
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:25.290
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:35.340
<i>The Black Brothers and the Wolf Pack smuggled Alfredo and Bianca into the palace.</i>

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:43.190
<i>With Romeo watching over him, Alfredo put his life on the line.</i>

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.180
<i>Romeo now awaits Alfredo's meeting with the King.</i>

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.180
Episode 29:

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.180
Forever Alfredo

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.410
They're late. I'm getting nervous.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.650
I'm to blame if something goes wrong.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:11.800
Don't be silly. Romeo's with Alfredo.
Things can't...

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.770
If Madam Monteverni weren't here, I'd have you all thrown in prison.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.310
So don't show your faces in here again!

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.210
What a grouch!

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.690
Romeo!

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.300
How'd it go?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.040
Alfredo and Bianca were on their way to see the King.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.080
So then...

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.550
He's probably telling the King the truth at this very moment.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.060
He did it! Alfredo finally did it!

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.290
Did it!

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.110
We did it, eh, Romeo?

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.100
Yeah.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.780
<i>Do your best, Alfredo.</i>

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.310
To be slandered in the presence of the King,

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:06.440
...and about an heirloom of my father...

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.840
This is not at all amusing, even as a child's prank!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.110
Then, Count Martini, I take it the medal pinned on your chest...

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.900
It is the Martini medal. Yes.
Given to me by my brother Vittorio.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.720
No it is not! My father's medal is right here, I assure you.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:28.900
Your Majesty, I'm sorry to have to say this, but...

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.970
Alfredo was rebellious...

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.540
...and no end of trouble to his father, even as an infant...

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.410
That's not true! Alfredo's...!

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:42.610
Bianca Martini! Mind your manners before the King.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.360
Yes, Ma'am.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.870
You'll have your turn after Count Martini has spoken his piece.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.300
Eternally grateful, Countess Isabella.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.400
I merely wish to hear what the Count has to say...

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.100
...so that His Majesty can make a fair judgment.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.720
It seems then, Countess, that you're pleading the case of these children?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.140
This is not a trial.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:11.020
We are merely trying to discover who is the righteous lover of truth,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.860
...and who is the low-down skunk up to his neck in lies.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:18.280
I agree... that's exactly what I wish to discover.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.710
Count Mauricio, please proceed.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:22.790
Yes, Sire.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.400
We were shocked when Alfredo set fire to his house...

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:29.120
...out of spite for his father, who had loved him so much.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:35.400
Unhappily, my brother Vittorio and my sister Fatricia lost their lives.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.980
And in the meantime Alfredo ran away.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.420
I'm told he's been sweeping chimneys ever since!

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.900
Sweeping chimneys?!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.800
Are you a chimney sweep?

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:47.900
Yes.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.000
Soot and ashes are his chums!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.440
If I may speak, Your Majesty?

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:05.530
I've never been ashamed of sweeping chimneys.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.970
Even though you were born into nobility?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.700
Yes... there's no difference between chimney sweeps and nobility.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.200
How dare you say that!

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.860
Wait, I want to hear what he has to say.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.540
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.490
Now then, Alfredo, what do you mean by that?

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.370
First, let me apologize for my careless words.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:30.700
I found true friendship for the first time as a chimney sweep.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.890
It's getting cold...

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.160
It'll be okay. He'll be fine.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.770
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.120
<i>I'm waiting to hear the good news, Alfredo.</i>

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.240
Snow...!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.740
They're all chimney sweeps, like me.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.740
They work hard every day, covered head to toe in soot and ashes.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.150
But however hard it gets, they never lose hope.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:03.240
That's because they believe in each other!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.060
The sacredness of the trust of others...

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.290
...and the beauty of trusting others...

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.770
Nobility and chimney sweeps esteem these two things above all others.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:20.590
That's what I learned from them, and I'm proud to say it.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.400
Nikita.
- Giovanni! I thought you'd gone home.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:37.400
Same here... but if I did, I wouldn't be able to sleep a wink.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.960
I hope he's careful.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.910
Alfredo Martini, if what you've said is not true...

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.690
I'm prepared for the consequences.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.540
Then you don't withdraw your accusation?

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.810
There is only one truth.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.360
Very well then. I've made my decision.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.920
The person passing off a fake for the real medal...

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.500
...is our "low-down skunk up to his neck in lies."

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:14.010
Please, do. Inspect this medal which is untainted by lies.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:29.160
Your Majesty's father awarded that medal to Vittorio 21 years ago.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:30.080
Indeed.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.360
My father marshaled his forces at Custoza against the Austrian army.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:38.350
In the midst of that fierce battle...

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:46.460
That young officer was Vittorio Martini.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:50.630
Because he saved my father's life, the battle ended in victory.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.940
Precisely so. I've heard the story many times from my brother.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.040
Count Mauricio, didn't your brother say anything else to you?

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:01.010
Eh?

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.740
...about a certain mark?

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.800
A mark, Your Majesty?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.560
The mark of benediction.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.810
Mark of benediction?

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:15.620
When Your Majesty's father gave this medal to my father,

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:18.270
...he also gave him a mark of benediction.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.610
You risked your life to save mine.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:27.500
In return for that honorable act,

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:33.390
...I'll carve a benediction on this medal.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:37.600
Your Majesty's father carved a mark upon this medal.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.260
It was a lifelong source of pride for my father.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:45.640
That's right. But there is no mark on the back of this medal!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.810
This is the mark of benediction.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.940
Your Majesty, please confirm it.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:09:00.140
No mistake about it. This is the medal my father gave to Vittorio.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:08.340
There's... there's been some kind of mistake!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.300
The boy must have switched the medals!

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:14.270
You're being disgraceful, Grazela.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.120
You didn't even know about the mark.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.470
You still think you can get away with this?

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:24.850
Mauricio! What are you doing? Say something!

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:30.010
Grazela... you goaded me on to do this to begin with.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:37.440
Are you trying to put the blame on me for everything?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.950
Let this be a warning:

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:50.510
God's anger falls down on dark deeds in every age.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.690
Throw those two out!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.640
Alfredo...

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.460
Do you think Mother and Father are looking down approvingly at us?

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:11.210
Yes.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:19.230
<i>Mother... Father...
It's finally over.</i>

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:24.430
<i>But I've exhausted all my life in getting here.</i>

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:29.460
<i>I don't have the strength to look after Bianca.</i>

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:43.390
Alfredo, Bianca, there you are.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.750
The King is waiting for you.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.360
Yes, Countess Isabella.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:49.250
Let's go, Bianca.
- OK.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.260
Say, Romeo...

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:05.250
I guess Alfredo might not come back now.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:11.650
After he's avenged his father, he doesn't need to come back.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.070
He's nobility, after all.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:31.530
What, so that's "goodbye"?

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:35.270
Dante, Alfredo doesn't need to come back...

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:41.160
It's true... The King likes him...
Maybe he'll get to go home.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.920
Do you all believe that?

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:45.550
Romeo.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.260
Alfredo will come back, won't he?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.240
Well, Romeo?

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.110
I don't know...

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.150
Romeo!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.240
Sure, I also want him to come back...

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:02.250
But if going home with Bianca would make him happy,

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:04.590
...I won't stop him.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:08.760
We were happy because he was here with us, after all.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.890
Now it's his turn.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.140
If it'll make Alfredo happy, I'm satisfied with that.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:17.790
Me too, Romeo.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:19.360
Me too.
- Me too.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.160
And me.
- Same here.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.020
Me too.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.620
Oh well... me too.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.550
It'll be lonely without him, though.

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.000
Sorry I'm late!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.150
Alfredo! You came back.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.460
This is the only home I've got.
You know that.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:43.960
I'm a chimney sweep, like the rest of you.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.540
Alfredo!

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.220
Romeo!

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:52.420
Alfredo!
- Alfredo!

00:12:55.200 --> 00:13:00.910
Thank you... It's thanks to you guys that the truth was revealed.

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:03.880
Thank goodness.
Thank goodness, Alfredo.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.510
He won't give up.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:39.240
About Alfredo... You said he's got the same sickness that killed my Dad.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:39.880
Yes...

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:42.920
It'll take more than that to do him in!

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.940
I'm going to beat him.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.850
That's right...
Alfredo's bound to be okay.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.640
I'm looking forward to our next fight.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.910
Man, we can do anything if we try.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.040
Like Alfredo always told us:

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:08.990
...friends can do anything if they work together.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.150
This is great!

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.570
Uh-oh... Gotta get going.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:18.340
You guys... We'll be friends forever.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:37.870
Do I have to go?

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:42.760
You promised not to make a fuss about staying at Dr. Casella's house.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:46.150
But tonight I want to be with you, big brother.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.870
I like little girls who listen to what their big brothers say.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.110
Hmph. You're so mean.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.500
I can go the rest of the way by myself.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.540
That was a quick change of mood.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.650
I don't want you to be mad at me, big brother.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.260
See you tomorrow.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.510
Bianca...

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.020
Big brother...

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.300
Sorry. I'm just happy about what happened tonight.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.070
Good night, Bianca.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.770
Good night, big brother.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.510
Good night, Romeo.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.760
Good night.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.840
Romeo... shall we tell God about the night's events?

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:55.720
Sure.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:02.070
<i>Romeo had by no means forgotten about Alfredo's illness.</i>

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:07.580
<i>But he had suppressed his fears until Alfredo's innocence had been proven.</i>

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.850
Alfredo's not going to get better.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:19.830
<i>But, watching Alfredo's tranquil face, Romeo couldn't believe it.</i>

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:28.360
<i>He had no idea that soon he and Alfredo would be separated forever.</i>

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:33.370
Do you remember the day we met, Romeo?

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:36.360
Yes.
- You gave me an apple...

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.790
He gave me these as a token of apology. Take one.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.380
OK, I'll take it.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:47.740
My name's Romeo. What's yours?

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.340
Hey... Isn't that you?

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:05.480
And despite that, you came running after me...

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:08.810
Holding on to that apple as if your life depended on it.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:15.860
That apple's really tasty. Eat it. It'll pick your spirits up.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.340
You ran all this way just for that?

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:20.890
Don't you want it?

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:27.460
Thanks.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.300
That's better.

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:32.790
You're a weird guy.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:37.240
That's right, and ever since that day I've been leaning on you for help!

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.350
Oh, I tried becoming more independent,

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.860
...but you're a tough act to follow.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.970
Romeo, you really don't get it, do you.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.260
I'm the one who's been dependent on you.

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:52.980
You've been my heart's support.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.320
Alfredo.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:07.700
Romeo... I don't know how I would have turned out if I hadn't met you.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:12.070
I might have led a shallow existence, obsessed only with revenge.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:17.380
I made it this far because you've been there.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:18.990
Thanks, Romeo.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:25.840
What's come over you, Alfredo?
You're embarrassing me... I'm not...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:31.020
Say, Alfredo... I'll be going home when winter's over.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.900
Why don't you and Bianca come visit me then?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:38.340
Sonogno is so beautiful in the spring.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:48.920
Big brother! Look at all the flowers!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.670
Let's do that, Alfredo. Wouldn't you...

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:02.350
Alfredo! So you were still sick after all.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.100
Wait, I'll call Dr. Casella.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:07.440
Romeo... Don't.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:11.230
But...
- Stay here with me.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.410
But Alfredo...
- Please...

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:21.390
Your Sonogno is a pretty little village...

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:25.000
But I have to go now.

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.920
Go where?

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.690
To Mother and Father.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:33.250
My time has come.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:37.280
But... That can't be!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:42.620
What about our promise to follow our dream when we grow up?

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:49.430
I'm sorry, Romeo... I won't be growing up.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:55.000
No! No!!

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.440
I don't want to be separated from you!

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.280
I... I want to grow up with you.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:08.710
<i>Dear God... please...</i>

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.840
<i>...just a little more strength.</i>

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.040
Romeo.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:22.200
We'll always be together.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.230
No matter how far apart.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:34.410
We'll always be together, no matter how far apart.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.760
Alfredo! Hang on!

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:46.510
Thank you, Romeo.
You were hope itself to me.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.620
No! Alfredo! Don't...!

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:55.460
Please carry on for me... see and do the things I would have...

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:00.440
...the dreams I never...

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:07.430
Take care of Bianca...

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:15.500
Alfredo.

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.140
Alfredo.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:24.430
The dreams you never what, Alfredo? You didn't finish.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.780
Alfredo!

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:36.240
Alfredo!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:58.900
<i>Alfredo's departure was far too sudden.</i>

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:04.450
<i>Dante sees me mooning around, and challenges me to a duel.</i>

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:08.130
<i>You're casting me out of the Black Brothers?</i>

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.610
See you then!

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.610
<i>The Last Promise</i>

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.610
Next time:

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:17.840
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:30.550
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:34.850
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:39.050
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.250
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:52.060
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:59.360
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:04.960
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.160
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
